                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I cannot give Riptale a good review. The base game is quite fun, but I have to give a negative review because of my experience playing on hard mode. Play this game, get every achievement except the last one. The hard mode has a lot jank, and you'll die to things that just are not your fault.\nWhether its the lingering projectiles after exiting and re-entering a room, or having my dashes go straight through enemies, or when the enemies in the underground forest kill me over and over with their unpredictable movements, or when enemies in a room I've never been in camp the entrance and instakill me upon entry, there is a lot that makes hard mode unfun.\nOn top of that, restarting runs to find a double HP shrine is a miserable process. None of the bosses are of any concern except for maybe the twins. \nThe music also got annoying after 10 hours. \nAll of which is a shame, since I love the way this game plays overall. Could have easily made the hard mode difficult another way, other than forcing you to complete the same game on 1HP. How about enemy movement speed? Or having enemies deal more hearts? Or enemies per room? \n6/10 game",
